{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/767898-keystones-as-anchors-for-a-high-psyche","id":767898,"title":"Keystones as anchors for a high Psyche?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-17T09:54:49-08:00","id":767898,"title":"Keystones as anchors for a high Psyche?","content":"Hey guys, it's Korogra after a long time of silence ( as per usual for me, but many of you know that.), how are all of you? I have been working on a very long, very expansive Geist campaign over the course of three + years, and not to spoil too much for those in my group who do troll the forums for when it is finally finished and I play it with them; one of the plot points involves a character who has achieved a high level of Psyche and at the behest of a vision of the future and the mythos of his Krewe binds his identity to his own keystone in the hopes of creating an even greater union between him and the Geist he is bound to in the form of making it his anchor as well. Even though I have fleshed out exactly what happens to the this character I am curious- what do you all think the outcome of such an action would be? Even if you believe that mechanically nothing would be different aside from a potentially indestructible anchor, I am excited to hear your theories on the matter!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T11:29:31-08:00","id":767967,"title":"","content":"Interesting idea, but I feel that an anchor for a high Psyche Sin Eater would probably need to be in something of the living world, to keep him/her from wandering too far into the land of the dead. A keystone is, by its very nature bound to a Geist and thus part of the dead. It's always house-ruleable, of course, but I feel that might require some kind of weakness to not be an instant +1 option to the players' stats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T11:36:06-08:00","id":767972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/767898-keystones-as-anchors-for-a-high-psyche?p=767967#post767967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting idea, but I feel that an anchor for a high Psyche Sin Eater would probably need to be in something of the living world, to keep him/her from wandering too far into the land of the dead. A keystone is, by its very nature bound to a Geist and thus part of the dead. It's always house-ruleable, of course, but I feel that might require some kind of weakness to not be an instant +1 option to the players' stats.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a good point, but I should point out the Keystone is as much of an anchor to the living world for the Geist as it is the &quot;unbeating heart&quot; of the creature, so it's still an object that represents a tie to the living world, it just so happens to be ghostly like the mini death god who's identity is tied to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T21:15:10-08:00","id":768274,"title":"","content":"Just a side question, is your game up anywhere?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-d